/* Watcom's OS/2 include tree keeps its extensionless C++ headers under 8.3
names -- "algorith", "stdexcep", "type_tra" -- so #include <algorithm> fails
even though the header is installed.  The filesystem is not the problem (long
names work fine here); this installation lost the long names, and Watcom's own
headers include each other by the short spellings.

The port therefore carries a directory of forwarders and puts it on the include
path first, which leaves the compiler's own tree untouched.  Anything that needs
a name longer than eight characters goes in here.
*/
#include <algorith>
